-- R8 does not rule on overloads, so a named site whose callee has more than one
-- definition in scope takes no default (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md section
-- 4.2; review silent F3, 2026-10-03). Before W4 the first #EVAL below was
-- ambiguous: neither `scaled` had every input it needs. It must stay so, and
-- not quietly become the first `scaled`, run on a presumed rate, when what the
-- author meant was the second and forgot `factor`.

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      factor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS base PLUS factor

-- ambiguous, as before W4: a named site that leaves out a defaulted input does
-- not choose the overload that has a default for it
#EVAL scaled WITH base IS 10

-- these two write every input one overload needs and are fine (11 and 20); the error above stops evaluation
#EVAL scaled WITH base IS 10, factor IS 1
#EVAL scaled WITH base IS 10, rate IS 2
